  "reading": "The feeder is exact: every window was fed its 4,080 slots and no slot was ever skipped. The loss of timing happens after it: 12,000-49,000 packets per run reached the socket after their slot (worst 114-291 ms), in idle and loaded windows alike, and were then sent at once, so their timing followed quinn's scheduling, not the grid; 172-1,652 full-size packets found no slot. Hypothesis (to test): quinn's congestion control (BBR) holds datagrams back when its estimate dips below the fixed stream rate. Next: a fixed-window controller on the client while the clock runs, judged by lateness falling to about zero."
 },
