  "reading": "Lateness fell from 12,000-49,000 packets per run (worst 114-291 ms) to 39-68 (worst 2-4 ms): quinn's congestion control was what held packets back. But 54,000-55,400 full-size packets per run found no slot and left on quinn's timing; run 1 leaked (gap spread p 0.0005).",
  "cause": "Reproduced on loopback with fq (a cloak test in its own network namespace): 2,453 of 16,465 packets found no slot in 4 s, against 12 without fq. Packets fq holds for their departure time count against the socket's send buffer; when it filled, sendmsg failed, quinn retried the packet, and the paced socket had already spent that packet's slot. Fix: a failed send puts its slot back, and the socket asks for a send buffer large enough for the look-ahead (capped by net.core.wmem_max). Unslotted packets: 14-17 per 16,440 with the fix; 342 with both halves removed; buffer only 14, slot restore only 114. Regression test the_clock_keeps_every_packet_on_its_slot_under_fq, run in CI under unshare -Urn with fq on loopback."
 },
