  "reading": "Two effects of opposite sign mix. With normal power management, loaded windows are smoother (gap spread AUC 0.71-0.89; leak 2 of 3): an idle CPU in deep sleep or at low frequency releases packets less evenly. With shallow sleep, loaded windows are rougher (AUC 0.27-0.33 on the largest gap or gap spread; leak 2 of 3 for qos): contention shows through, probably because the kernel's release of paced packets competes with the load on the same cores. Fixed frequency comes closest (2 of 3 clean); both together gave no significant leak in 2 valid runs but still lean. No setting removes the signal entirely. The effects are microseconds on a quiet virtual link timestamped at the first hop: a strong lab adversary. Whether they survive a real path's millisecond jitter is the question for the real-website run. Base runs leaned harder here than in the earlier wire-clock runs (0.61-0.64), so conditions move this signal."
 },
 "downstream_collapse": {
  "setup": "tools/wf_real.py collect --config fast with AVPN_WIRE_CLOCK_PPS=4000 AVPN_CATCH_UP_MS=50, the re-run's pinning (client and browser on cores 0,1; relay, exit and capture on 2,3) and fq on the client link; 4 sites x 2 loads; both cloaks' QUIC path (cwnd, RTT) sampled every 5 s from outside the lab",
  "real_run": "Real-website re-run 2026-11-15, clock passes: round 1 had 1 of 40 loads ok, round 2 none (every load dnsNotFound). Live in round 2: the relay's cloak handed QUIC about 4,000 datagrams/s for the client, the client's cloak received about 170/s (4%); the client's carrier, given no real data back, was restarted every 10-12 s. The fast pass of the same round delivered 85% (no clock).",
  "mechanism": "The handshake is not paced, so quinn's minimum RTT is the link's (81-96 us in the lab). Afterwards every acknowledgement from the client rides in a packet the clock holds for up to its 30 ms look-ahead, so the relay sees about 27 ms. BBR's window is bandwidth x minimum RTT: it shrank to 8-11 packets and never grew back.",
  "fix": "src/cloak.rs server_config_clocked: a clocked chain's server sends with the fixed window too (as the clocked client already did). The downstream's rate is the carrier's, set by the signed class, as on WireGuard over UDP. Test: a_clocked_chains_server_never_shrinks_its_window (fails with BBR).",
